| Spike 2 driver: runs the nine steps in order. /delay is in tenths of a second.
Sub Main
    | Step 1
    /lua run spike2_recorder
    /delay 10
    | Step 2: start target, let it run
    /lua run spike2_target
    /delay 50
    | Step 3: pause
    /lua pause spike2_target
    /delay 50
    | Step 4: resume
    /lua pause spike2_target
    /delay 30
    | Step 5: manual stop
    /lua stop spike2_target
    /delay 30
    | Step 6: run and let it finish by itself (target runs 20 seconds)
    /lua run spike2_target
    /delay 250
    | Step 7: same name again (new PID), then stop it
    /lua run spike2_target
    /delay 50
    /lua stop spike2_target
    /delay 10
    | Step 8: deliberate crash (red error text expected)
    /lua run spike2_crash
    /delay 60
    | Step 9
    /lua stop spike2_recorder
/return
